  <h2>Guided Tours Are Mandatory</h2>
  <p>The DMZ is an active military zone — independent visits are not permitted. You must join an organized tour. Tours depart from central Seoul (usually Hongik University Station or major hotels) and include transportation, guide, and entry fees.</p>

  <h2>Tour Types</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Half-day tour</strong> (4–5 hours): Imjingak + 3rd Tunnel + Dora Observatory. Good for tight schedules.</li>
    <li><strong>Full-day tour</strong> (8–9 hours): All sites including Panmunjeom/JSA. The definitive experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Private tour</strong>: Custom itinerary, smaller groups, more flexibility.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to Bring</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>🪪 <strong>Passport — mandatory.</strong> Military ID check at the entrance. No passport = no entry.</li>
    <li>👟 Comfortable walking shoes (tunnel involves steep slopes)</li>
    <li>🧥 Layers — it's often colder near the border</li>
    <li>📷 Camera (restrictions vary by site)</li>
    <li>💵 Cash for lunch, coffee, and souvenirs at Imjingak</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rules & Restrictions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow your guide at all times — this is non-negotiable in a military zone</li>
    <li>Photography prohibited at certain spots (guide will specify)</li>
    <li>Dress code at Panmunjeom: no ripped jeans, no revealing clothing, no military-style clothing</li>
    <li>Children under 11 are not permitted at some DMZ sites</li>
    <li>No going off-path, no approaching fences</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Getting There</h2>
  <p>The DMZ is approximately 60km north of Seoul — about 1.5 hours by coach. All tours include return transport. Departure points are typically at Hongik University Station (AREX line, convenient from Incheon Airport) or Gyeongbokgung area hotels.</p>

  <div class="tip-box">
    💡 <strong>Book JSA separately:</strong> The Joint Security Area (Panmunjeom) requires advance booking with UN approval and fills up weeks in advance. Book as early as possible if this is your priority.
  </div>
